Environment: macOS 26.6.1, Apple M5 Max (AArch64, 18 logical CPUs), Rust 1.85.0, Maven 3.10.0 with OpenJDK 27.

## Phase 18 code changes already committed at this revision

- Preserved Java's signed synchronous RPC timeout ordering: connect/reuse first, subtract elapsed whole milliseconds, and send no frame when the remaining timeout is nonpositive. Core runtime lookup methods now retain signed i32 timeouts.
- Added `MQClientApi` access to the shared remoting client and a lock-scoped mutable NameServer address-list adapter, preserving Java getter/list alias behavior without exposing an unlocked mutable reference.
- Focused runtime, remoting, API-surface, and timeout regressions were already run during those implementation commits. Current workspace validation below covers the committed changes together.

## Validation

- `cargo test --offline --workspace --locked` passed. An initial attempt had a codec test child remain at macOS `dyld` startup with no Rust test code running; it was interrupted, the isolated codec suite passed (8/8), and a complete workspace rerun passed.
